way back in the summer of last year mark  german gave us a bombshell leak claiming  that apple is working on a redesign of  the ipad pro with a glass back for the  2022 release  yes i said glass back just like we've  had for years with the iphone and if  you're wondering why in the world apple  would do this well it's because apple  apparently wants to enable wireless  charging on the back of the ipad pro  which might sound a bit ridiculous but  the plan is actually genius first of all  mark says it'll support both wireless  charging and reverse wireless charging  kind of like what we currently have with  apple's mac safe power bank where you  can plug in a cable to charge your  iphone and your iphone will reverse  wireless charge the power bank but  apple's plan for the ipad pro is even  better because according to mark german  you're going to be able to recharge your  iphone your earpods and even your future  apple watch by using this new reverse  wireless charging feature on the back of  the ipad pro and if you're wondering how  that's gonna work the only answer is mac  save charging by using the mac safe puck  which mark german has already mentioned  so that you can use your ipad in the  upright position potentially with the  magic keyboard while also recharging  your devices magnetically using mac safe  at the same time and that actually makes  a lot of sense because both the airpods  3 and the airpods pro have recently been  updated with max safe charging support  which works great and i even made a  recent video discussing how apple could  easily build maxsafe into the next gen  magic keyboard as well so we can pass  through charge with multiple stacks of  coils so definitely watch that video but  with all that said if you think a full  glass back on an ipad pro is a little  insane because it's much more  susceptible to drops and cracks well you  are right because it has been reported  that apple hit a major roadblock and  plans to redesign the ipad pro and  according to 925 mac this glass back  ipad pro redesign may have been scrapped  because apple was concerned that the  ipad would become too fragile due to all  of the glass so unfortunately it looks  like the upcoming 2022 ipad pro is most  likely not gonna come with that full  glass back redesign but wait the story  doesn't end there because apple might  have an even better trick up their  sleeve according to 95 max sources apple  has actually been developing ipad pro  prototypes with large apple logos that  are made out of glass instead of metal  and if you think that's crazy 925 mac  pointed out that apple increased the  size of the apple logos on the new  macbook pros almost like they knew that  they were thinking of doing the same  thing for the ipad pro as well but  getting back to the potential glass  apple logo design this actually makes a  lot of sense because the glass would  allow wireless charging power to be  distributed through it and then as for  the max safe magnets the aluminum back  wouldn't matter at all because the ipad  pro already uses a ton of magnets for  connecting to the magic keyboard and  then of course the major benefit is that  the rest of the back will remain being  built out of metal so it's gonna be much  more durable and then getting into more  of the details they confirmed that one  of the prototypes featured magsafe  support which makes total sense but this  time with stronger magnets than you get  with the iphone to prevent accidental  damage so stronger magnets make a lot of  sense since you don't want your air pods  or even your iphone falling off of the  back of the ipad pro while charging and  then going even further they mentioned  that the magsafe charger will support  faster wireless charging speeds compared  to the 15 watts you get with the iphone  and this makes a lot of sense because  the ipad pro's battery is much larger  and takes more time to charge so apple  will either have an updated max safe  charger with faster 