then going back to my renders i also had  one more detail that you may have missed  the smart connector that we currently  have on the ipad pro is now gone on my  new renders of the 2022 ipad pro and the  reason i did that is because i fully  believe that the new ipad pro is going  to be able to power the magic keyboard  case using reverse wireless charging  through the mac safe connector so there  won't be any physical connectors at all  and if you think i'm totally crazy for  believing that i recently found some  ipad pro patents claiming that a new  future magic keyboard will come with two  sets of max safe charging coils  one set will be used for pass-through  charging the ipad pro and the second set  will be used to reverse wireless charge  accessories like an iphone air pods or  future apple watch and now on top of all  of that 9.5 mac did give us some extra  details like for example apple is  planning on increasing the battery size  on the new ipad pro to help offset the  loss and battery power when using the  magic keyboard especially since it's  going to be powered wirelessly in my  opinion so if you take all those rumors  and add them up together the whole idea  of going with the glass apple logo  actually makes the most sense because  from the outside you won't really notice  that it supports max life wireless  charging until you place the puck on  there or any of your other mac save  devices and you're not gonna risk any  damage from having a full glass back and  in terms of when we should expect this  new ipad pro i fully believe that it's  going to be coming this fall just based  on the one and a half year update cycle  that apple usually has for their ipad  pro especially since we're not expecting  the m2 chip to come out until the second  half of this year so with all that said  if you think the larger glass apple logo  is a good idea then go ahead and click  the circle about to subscribe for more  videos like this one and definitely  check out that 